===Alternative forms===
* [[take-away]]

===Etymology===
From {{compound|take|away|lang=en}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{context|chiefly|UK|Australia|and|New Zealand|of food|lang=en}} To be [[eaten]] off the [[premises]].

====Usage notes====
Frequently used in the question “eat-in or '''takeaway'''?” (North American: “for here or to go?”) at restaurants that offer food for both on and off premise eating.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to be eaten off premises}} [[to go]] {{qualifier|North America}}

====Antonyms====
* [[eat in]] {{qualifier|British}}
* [[for here]] {{qualifier|North America}}
* [[have here]] {{qualifier|New Zealand}}

====Descendants====
* Italian: {{l|it|takeaway}}

